# {{lb|en|linguistics}} A [[Spanish]] [[language]] item as it appears in another language.
#: {{syn|en|Hispanism|Castilianism}}
# {{rfdef|en}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Lewis Hanke|title=Modern Latin America: Continent in Ferment|year=1959|publisher=Van Nostrand|page=131|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=JGFKAAAAMAAJ&q=%22Hispanicism%22&dq=%22Hispanicism%22&hl=en&cd=19&source=gbs_api|passage=More recently there has burst forth an enthusiastic '''Hispanicism''', no longer the '''Hispanicism''' of Columbus Day with its odes to the great navigator, nor the '''Hispanicism''' of the bull fighters and the cabaret singers, but a historical  '''Hispanicism''' {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James W. Cortada|title=Spain in the Nineteenth-century World|year=1994|publisher=Greenwood Press|page=126|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=KitpAAAAMAAJ&q=%22Hispanicism%22&dq=%22Hispanicism%22&hl=&cd=17&source=gbs_api|isbn=978-0-313-27655-2|passage=One French writer argued that '''Hispanicism''' was a proper response to U.S.  expansionism, provided Spain could assure its sister Latin states in Europe (France and Italy) that their interests were not endangered.}}

